Package: mscc-portaudio
Version: 19.8.2
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Multus SDR / MSCC Linux <local@localhost>
Depends: libc6, libasound2 | libasound2t64, libpulse0
Recommends: pulseaudio-utils, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio
Homepage: https://www.portaudio.com/
Description: PortAudio with Pulse+ALSA for MSCC (Raspberry Pi OS arm64)
 Prebuilt PortAudio 19.x shared library with PulseAudio and ALSA host
 APIs, installed under /usr/local for Multus MSCC servers.
 .
 Use this instead of (or alongside) Debian libportaudio2 when you need
 Pulse devices such as VirtualA / VirtualB for digi modes.
 .
 After install, ldconfig registers /usr/local/lib. Rebuild or install
 MSCC binaries linked with rpath to /usr/local (mscc 1.0.23+).
 .
 Does not remove Debian libportaudio2; MSCC binaries should use rpath
 so they load this library.
